      "category": "Text",
      "text": "No liability is to be contracted for in excess of funds available for the purpose. The head of a department or other agency shall be held strictly accountable for exceeding appropriations without specific itemized approval of the Mayor. All balances of appropriations for which no contract liability is registered on the books of the Office of the Comptroller shall expire six months after the close of the 1973-1974 fiscal year and disposed of pursuant to law, except for encumbered balances in General Purchase Fund accounts, which shall expire one year after the close of the 1973-1974 fiscal year.",
